   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the elder law, in relation to information regarding the home\nenergy assistance program for participants in the elderly pharmaceutical\ninsurance coverage program",
    "basePrintNo": "S796",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S796-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §245, Eld L (as proposed in S.8760-A & A.9369-A)",
    "lawSection": "Elder Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S796\n\nSPONSOR: CLEARE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the elder law, in relation to information regarding the\nhome energy assistance program for participants in the elderly pharma-\nceutical insurance coverage program\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis chapter amendment clarifies the provisions of L.2024, c.633,\nregarding the dissemination of information about the Home Energy Assist-\nance Program for participants in the Elderly Pharmaceutical Insurance\nCoverage Program\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter regarding the dissem-\nination of information about the Home Energy Assistance Program for\nparticipants in the Elderly Pharmaceutical Insurance Coverage Program.\n\nThis legislation eliminates the automatic identification and enrollment\nin the HEAP program for participants in the Elderly Pharmaceutical\nInsurance Coverage Program. Instead, the chapter amendment emphasizes\nenhanced interagency information sharing to more effectively enroll\neligible individuals in HEAP.\n\nSubsection 2 amends the underlying chapter requiring the Department of\nHealth (DOH) to notify program participants and provide information on\nHEAP eligibility and application procedures with each application\ndistributed, as well as annually to all program participants.\n\nSubsection 3 amends the underlying legislation requiring the DOH to\nconsult with the Office of Temporary and Disability Assistance (OTDA)\nand the New York State Office for the Aging (NYSOFA) when developing a\nprocess to notify EPIC program participants about HEAP eligibility and\napplication procedures.\n\nSubsection 4 amends the underlying chapter by transferring the responsi-\nbility of providing written notifications and information to households\nthat apply for and are enrolled in HEAP to the relevant local social\nservices districts. The notifications and information must comply with\nOTDA regulations.\n\nSubsection 5 amends the underlying chapter to allow OTDA and DOH to\ncollaborate in establishing any necessary rules and regulations for\nimplementing the provisions of this legislation.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 633 of the Laws of 2024. S.8760-A passed\nthe Senate in June 2024 and A.9369-A passed the Assembly in May 2024.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2024 amending the Elder Law relating to the auto-\nmatic identification and enrollment of Elderly Pharmaceutical Insurance\nCoverage Program enrollees in the Home Energy Assistance Program, as\nproposed in legislative bills numbers S. 8760-A and A.  9369-A, takes\neffect.\n",
